# Terminal emulator preference order for xdg-terminal-exec.
#
# Omarchy launches every terminal it spawns through xdg-terminal-exec
# (see omarchy-launch-terminal), so this file is what decides which terminal
# opens when you edit a config from the menu, run a floating command, etc.
#
# xdg-terminal-exec prefers ${XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP,,}-xdg-terminals.list over
# the generic xdg-terminals.list. Under Hyprland that means this file shadows
# ~/.config/xdg-terminals.list entirely — setting only the generic one has no
# effect here. Omarchy's own default ships foot.desktop.
com.mitchellh.ghostty.desktop
